From: Neutron lab (fx49) 
Subject: [PATCH] nvcuda: cuD3D11GetDevice/cuD3D11GetDevices answer by adapter LUID, like Windows

What he saw (Neutron#49): a hybrid laptop (Radeon 760M + RTX 5050) where Premiere's export
loads the CPU. This patch is a Windows-parity fix found on the way, not the cause of that.

Mechanism: wine_cuD3D11GetDevice was a semi-stub. For ANY DXGI adapter -- the AMD/Intel GPU
of a hybrid laptop too -- it returned CUDA_SUCCESS and device 0, and stored that adapter's LUID
as a global override that cuDeviceGetLuid then returned for every device. So asking "which CUDA
device drives the AMD adapter?" answered "the NVIDIA one" and then made the NVIDIA device report
the AMD LUID. cuD3D11GetDevices was an unimplemented stub (calling it crashed the caller).

Windows: cuD3D11GetDevice returns the CUDA device whose LUID equals the adapter's, and
CUDA_ERROR_NO_DEVICE (100) for an adapter no CUDA device drives; cuD3D11GetDevices does the same
for the adapter of a D3D11 device. Now: each CUDA device's LUID is read from the same registry key
cuDeviceGetLuid already reads (win32u writes it next to the Vulkan UUID) and compared with the
adapter's. The LUID override stays, but only for the matched device. If no device's LUID can be
read at all, the old answer (device 0) is kept for an NVIDIA adapter only.

Not covered: cuD3D10GetDevice, cuD3D9GetDevice and cuD3D11CtxCreate still use device 0 (unchanged).
Multi-NVIDIA machines are untested (one NVIDIA GPU in the lab).

Lab (runtime 11.10-186fx = 186 + this, Premiere 26.5.2.5, emulated hybrid: lavapipe presented as
a Radeon 760M + __NV_PRIME_RENDER_OFFLOAD=1; probe = gpuprobe + cuD3D11GetDevices per adapter):
  fix, n=2: GetDevice(NVIDIA) -> 0 dev 0, LUID 3f7; GetDevice(AMD) -> 100, LUID stays 3f7;
            GetDevices(NVIDIA device) -> 0, 1 device; GetDevices(AMD device) -> 100, 0 devices.
  NEUTRON_CUDA_D3D_ANY_ADAPTER=1, n=2, same build: GetDevice(AMD) -> 0 dev 0 and cuDeviceGetLuid(0)
            becomes the AMD LUID 3f6 (= 11.10-186).
  Premiere on the fix: CUDA renderer offered and current; 28 exports (13 sequences x2 + MRQ x2)
            all on the GPU path, same CPU cost as 186 (p0 4.5-6 CPU-s, 6-track 22-30 CPU-s per 30 s).

Kill switch: NEUTRON_CUDA_D3D_ANY_ADAPTER=1 (old cuD3D11GetDevice semi-stub and global LUID override).
